Subject: [PATCH] fix(capacityAdapter): remove unconditional slice(0,6) in vision trimmer

Bug: The capacityAdapter.vision trimmer in chunk 112.js unconditionally
slices the conversation head to 6 messages BEFORE checking the token
budget. This discards the middle of the conversation (e.g. user's
current task) whenever the head exceeds 6 non-system messages, even
when the model's context window has plenty of room (e.g. Gemini 1M).

Symptom: vision requests with images get routed to models like
gemini-3.7-flash, but the context sent has only: system + 6 earliest
messages + tail. Any task defined after message 6 is dropped, causing
the model to answer an old unrelated topic (typically SSH test from
session preamble).

Fix: Change `o = l.slice(0, 6)` to `o = l.slice()` so all leading
messages are kept. The existing budget-based pop loop
(`for (; p > n && o.length > 0;) p -= k(m(o.pop()))`) already handles
the case where the budget is actually exceeded.

This is a one-character fix (removing the ", 6" argument). The budget
formula `n = 0.8 * contextWindow * 4` characters still guards against
over-long payloads.
---
 app/.next-cli-build/server/chunks/112.js | 2 +-
 1 file changed, 1 insertion(+), 1 deletion(-)

diff --git a/app/.next-cli-build/server/chunks/112.js b/app/.next-cli-build/server/chunks/112.js
--- a/app/.next-cli-build/server/chunks/112.js
+++ b/app/.next-cli-build/server/chunks/112.js
@@
-let n=.8*(b||2e5)*4,o=l.slice(0,6),p=f.concat(o,j).reduce((a,b)=>a+k(m(b)),0)
+let n=.8*(b||2e5)*4,o=l.slice(),p=f.concat(o,j).reduce((a,b)=>a+k(m(b)),0)
